<h1>Outline Pages</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US">The</span> <span class="Command">Outline Pages</span> <span lang="EN-US">command is accessible from</span> <b><span class="Path">Pages &gt; Outline Pages</span></b> in <span class="Mode">Inspection</span> <span lang="EN-US">mode.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">This command allows creating outlines for associated pages. It works for 3D view as well as for 2D sections. The outlines appear as red squares in a 2D section and as red cube in the 3D view. This command will be grayed if no pages are available in the pages list.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">Double-click on the page where other pages will be outlined and call the command. The following dialog box will appear:</span></p>
<p><img src="../images/outline_pages.gif" width="401px" height="284px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">All available report pages, except the current one, are shown in the left window. Select one or more pages and use the right arrow button to move them to the outline window. All pages for outlining are shown in the right window. Left arrow is used to move pages from the outline window to the left window. Use</span> <span class="Shortcut">Shift</span> <span lang="EN-US">from the keyboard for multiple page selection. When ready press the OK button.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP504103250" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/IMAGE037.GIF" width="865px" height="685px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Zoom Area 1 page</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">is ready to be included as outlined in the</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>General</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">page.</span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p><img src="../images/IMAGE038.GIF" width="865px" height="685px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Zoom Area 2 page</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">is ready to be included as outlined in the</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>General</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">page.</span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p><img src="../images/IMAGE039.GIF" width="865px" height="685px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Zoom Area 1 page</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">and</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Zoom Area 2 page</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">are outlined in the</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>General</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">page.</span></p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-US">To remove later outlined pages double-click on the page with outlined pages and call</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Outline Pages</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">command. In the dialog select one or more pages from the right-hand window and use the left arrow button to move them to the left-hand window. Use</span> <span class="Shortcut">Shift</span> <span lang="EN-US">from the keyboard for multiple page selection. When ready press the OK button. Outlining of the removed pages will disappear from the current page.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">Colour of outlining can be customised from</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours</b></span><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>

